-- title:
--   Valuation property of the localized modular ring at level q
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the coefficientwise images of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)`, the latter being the subfield of $\mathbb Q(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor expansions of level $1\cdot q$ (the level is written in the factored form $1 \cdot q$). Let $R$ be the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathfrak q)\!)$ generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with the two series $j(\mathfrak q)$ and $j(\mathfrak q^{\,q})$, and let $\mathcal O =$ `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red` be the localisation of $R$ away from the prime ideal `redKer` attached to $\mathrm{red}$: the set of Laurent series $f$ for which there exist $r, s \in R$ with $s \notin$ `redKer` and $f \cdot s = r$. The assertion is that for every $g \in F$, either $g \in \mathcal O$ or $g^{-1} \in \mathcal O$ (for $g = 0$ the first alternative holds).
--
--   This is the valuation-ring criterion for the local ring of the Kronecker plane model $A[j(\mathfrak q), j(\mathfrak q^{\,q})]$ at the generic point of the component of its characteristic-$q$ fibre passing through the cusp $\infty$: intersected with the function field of $X_0(q)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the localized modular ring satisfies the defining dichotomy of a valuation ring. It is used in the construction of the level-one prolongation pair and its two integral subrings, and in the existence of a nonzero localized reduction homomorphism in characteristic $q$.
